   </title>
   <document-link format="APPLICATION/PDF" url="https://www.adb.org/sites/default/files/project-documents/56368/56368-001-rrp-en.pdf">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Reports and Recommendations of the President</narrative>
    </title>
    <category code="A08"></category>
    <language code="EN"></language>
    <document-date iso-date="2025-07-31+08:00"></document-date>
   </document-link>
   <indicator measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">1.1. The government has issued the CIPP 2023&#x2013;2030 as the detailed decarbonization and energy transition action plan for Indonesia to achieve its 2030 greenhouse gas emissions target of capping the on-grid emissions at 250 million tons of CO2 including priority investment and financing plans for scaling up renewable energy capacity and early retirement of coal-fired power plants, strategy to ensure a just energy transition considering the socioeconomic impact, including on gender equality, enabling policy options and implementation framework. (CMMI)</narrative>
    </title>
   </indicator>
   <indicator measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">1.2. CMMI has issued a decision to establish the government&#x2019;s minister-level energy transition task force to supervise and monitor energy transition activities centrally, including activities stipulated in the CIPP. (CMMI)</narrative>
    </title>
   </indicator>
   <indicator measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">1.3. CMMI has issued a decree to establish a working team, consisting of senior management officials of CMMI, other related ministries and PLN, that regularly reports to the national energy transition taskforce to ensure implementation of energy transition activities with focus areas aligned with the CIPP. (CMMI)</narrative>
    </title>
   </indicator>
   <indicator measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">1.4. MEMR has approved and issued a regulation, eliminating capacity fees and establishing procedures to set the system quota of distributed electricity generation activities, especially for commercial and industrial sectors to increase the number of rooftop solar PV facility installations in Indonesia. (MEMR)</narrative>
    </title>
   </indicator>
   <indicator measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">1.5. MEMR has issued a ministerial regulation to establish the basis for carbon trading with emissions from coal-fired power plants connected to the PLN power systems as the initial priority, and a decree to assign emission ceiling to each power plant as an initial step of implementing a carbon trading market. d (MEMR)</narrative>
    </title>
   </indicator>
   <indicator measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">1.6. MEMR has issued a regulation providing incentives to accelerate the deployment of up to 50,000 units in 2023 and 150,000 units in 2024 of electric two-wheelers in the country. (MEMR)</narrative>
    </title>
   </indicator>
   <indicator measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">1.7. The Ministry of Finance has issued a regulation to set up the Energy Transition Platform for providing financing, including blended financing and international financial institution financing for energy transition investments including early retirement of coal-fired power plants and their replacement with renewable energy.</narrative>
    </title>
   </indicator>
   <indicator measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">20 Sep 2024 | News Release: https://www.adb.org/news/adb-approves-policy-loan-support-indonesia-energy-transition</narrative>
    </title>
   </indicator>
